[h1:customized-color-table [role cyan Customized color table]]

p* -> d* -> dd* -> ddd* -> dddd*

p: pure;

d: dark;

More d, more dark;

For example: ddred

The color names with no prefix d and no prefix p are preserved and not changed, those colors are provided by official boost quickbook. Such as red, provided by official boost quickbook.

[*code:]

[!teletype]
```
[role red Hello c++ !] - red by boost quickbook
[role dred Hello c++ !] - dred by this util
```

output:

[pre
[role red Hello c++ !] - red by boost quickbook
[role dred Hello c++ !] - dred by this util
]

[h2:color-table The Color Table]

[pre
red :
[role pred pred] [role dred dred] [role ddred ddred] [role dddred dddred] [role ddddred ddddred]

green :
[role pgreen pgreen] [role dgreen dgreen] [role ddgreen ddgreen] [role dddgreen dddgreen] [role ddddgreen ddddgree]

blue :
[role pblue pblue] [role dblue dblue] [role ddblue ddblue] [role dddblue dddblue] [role ddddblue ddddblue]

yellow (anti-blue) :
[role pyellow pyellow] [role dyellow dyellow] [role ddyellow ddyellow] [role dddyellow dddyellow] [role ddddyellow ddddyellow]

cyan (anti-red) :
[role pcyan pcyan] [role dcyan dcyan] [role ddcyan ddcyan] [role dddcyan dddcyan] [role ddddcyan ddddcyan]

magenta (anti-green) :
[role pmagenta pmagenta] [role dmagenta dmagenta] [role ddmagenta ddmagenta] [role dddmagenta dddmagenta] [role ddddmagenta ddddmagenta]

[role redpurple1 redpurple1] [role redpurple2 redpurple2]
[role greenpurple1 greenpurple1] [role greenpurple2 greenpurple2]
[role bluepurple1 bluepurple1] [role bluepurple2 bluepurple2]
]

[h1:quickbook-example [role cyan Quickbook Example]]

[h2:qbk-code Quickbook .qbk code:]

[!teletype]
```
[pre
[role dddgreen c++ is the most awesome programming language in the world !
Boot library is the most helpful and awesome c++ library !
Object-oriented programming is the most interesting programming of all programmings !]

[role dddred c++ is the most awesome programming language in the world !
